  "summary": "The bare ESP32-WROOM module itself: 18 x 25.5 mm, 3.1 mm tall, 38 castellated pads, RF shield can, PCB antenna. Solders flat onto a carrier board.",
  "confidence": "datasheet",
  "source": "Outline 18.00 x 25.50 mm and the 3.10 mm total height from the Espressif ESP32-WROOM-32E/32UE datasheet drawing; the pad pattern from KiCad's official ESP32-WROOM-32 footprint: 38 castellated pads, two rows of 14 on 1.27 mm pitch whose inner edge sits 1.5 mm from each long edge, 10 across the solder end and a 5 x 5 mm centre land, antenna keep-out marked 6.5 mm at that end. The 0.80 mm PCB and the 15.8 x 17.6 x 2.3 mm shield can are measured off KiCad's official 3D model of the module, where PCB plus can lands exactly on the datasheet's 3.10 mm; the can outline is not dimensioned on the datasheet drawing, so treat it as within about 0.4 mm. The preview shows the 38 peripheral castellated pads; the centre thermal land is omitted.",
